Z||000002||RaeQwan||10-28-2000||10:52 PM||||Archie doesn't do N* conversions does he?||||reg||1
Z||000003||RaeQwan||10-28-2000||10:52 PM||||Archie doesn't do N* conversions does he?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwanpenguin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bald Dude||10-28-2000||10:57 PM||||I guess I should have been clearer.  I want opinions on Archies conversion (using a small block) versus Design One using a Northstar.<P>Mark||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||10-28-2000||11:53 PM||||I guess it comes down to what do you want?  Are you looking for a streetable proven package with gobs of torque that can be worked on by any shadetree mechanic, or do you want high gee-whiz quotient when you pop the deck and show off those bg camshaft covers, along with a high maintainance overhead.  My personal opinion is that for the way 98% of us drive on American roads, torque is king, and pushrods rule...<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||10-29-2000||09:01 AM||||While working on a Northstar is expensive, it will never need to be worked on. The engines are reliable and bulletproof.<P>I looked at the Design One website and am not impressed. Their conversion looks like it involves 12 times as much work as it has to. It does not look well thought out, either.<P>You'd lose the bottom of your trunk! WTF is up with that?!?<P>They practically make a whole new cradle!<P>One picture shows the engine on the cradle with a single exhaust, one shows the back of a car with dual exhaust. Huh?<P>They bolt the dogbone to the back fo the firewall. I guess i'd have to see one in person, but that does not strike me as being a strong enough place for a dogbone.<P>Putting the coolant overflow tank in the back is interesting, but not necessary.<P>Why is the battery in the trunk? For $5,000, they should include a front mount battery kit.<P>Do you want handling? A Northstar with 4T80E trans weighs as much as an SBC with stickshift. Both will wreak havoc with your weight distribution.<P>I think that Archie's kit is much better thought out that Design One's. Similar levels of performance can result from each.<P>Look up my post "A northstar swap is easy as pie". <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005498.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005498.html</A>  <BR>You just might do a better job yourself.<P>"I like the idea of the Northstar with a 4 speed auto connected to a smog-legal motor."<P>Why did you put it that way?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||10-29-2000||12:32 PM||||The Northstar itself weighs about as much as a 2.8. It's the tranny that adds all of the weight. <BR>Design One charges an arm and a leg for their parts. $5 grand is one thing for a conversion, but $4-6 thousand more for the engine is laughable.<P>For $6000 Engine Master Conversions (32 W. Strathmore Ave. Pontiac MI 48340-2770) makes a RWD conversion kit (It's not a fiero swap) with an engine,(under 14,000 miles) Transmission (not transaxle), header building kit, a standalone Engine wiring harness w/ early Northstar computer. <P>They also sell the engines so if you talk to them, they might be able to sell most of the stuff to make your own Northstar conversion. for less than that. Especially if you follow Wills instructions.<P>*info out of Feb 2000 Car Craft<BR>Hope that my rambling is understandable.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||10-29-2000||02:35 PM||||I say be different and do a Norhtstar conversion. Do what makes you happy and don’t frown on the money. About the double overhead cam engines having no torque well I have a 2001 Toyota Tundra with a double overhead cam 32 valve v8 and it has gobs of low end torque and top end power. It has 315 ft. lbs. of torque at just 3400 rpm out of only 285 cubic inches or 4.7-liters of displacement. The old rules about only push rod motors having low-end power have been broken.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bald Dude||10-29-2000||07:31 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B><BR>"I like the idea of the Northstar with a 4 speed auto connected to a smog-legal motor."<P>Why did you put it that way?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah,  I guess I should have worded that better.  I should have said I want (need) a smog legal motor, and a Northstar would be smog legal.  However, <I>any</I> v-8 could be made smog legal for the nice govt folks here in PA.  <P>I'm not really concerned about handling problems with the motor being off center.  I could always beef up the passenger side rear suspension if I have to.  I'm looking for ease of assembly with a good design that is going to be reliable and powerful.<BR>  <BR>I have checked out Archie's site and am <I>very</I> impressed!  He seems to be the go-to guy in the 8 cylinder swap arena. His design does look very well thought out and fairly simple to complete.  I just wanted to cover all my bases and research all options before I plunk down a large chunk of change.  I have not read any reports of anyone doing a northstar swap.  I know they have been done 'cause I have seen the pictures.  I just wanted to know how the n-star swap compares.  <P>Thanks for the replies and opinions and wish me luck.<P>Mark<P><p>[This message has been edited by Bald Dude (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bald Dude||10-29-2000||07:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B><P>Look up my post "A northstar swap is easy as pie". <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005498.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005498.html</A>  <P>You just might do a better job yourself.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I looked up the thread indicated and found it to be very informative.  It is clear to me that Archie cares very much about his craft and the quality and saftey of the finished product.  <P>Thanks!<P>Mark||||reg||1
Z||000011||Will||10-30-2000||10:01 PM||||By "weight distribution" I meant front-rear, not side to side. Extra weight in the rear increases trailing throttle oversteer and power-on understeer.<BR>||||reg||1
